1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,170
A heart artery can narrow again inside a
stent.

2
00:00:03,495 --> 00:00:08,057
In selected cases, a drug-coated balloon
can treat that narrowing without leaving a

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:13,479
second metal scaffold. Here’s what happens
from the first images to the final check

4
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,686
and recovery.

5
00:00:15,197 --> 00:00:18,297
Coronary arteries carry blood to the heart
muscle.

6
00:00:18,576 --> 00:00:23,162
When a segment narrows again inside a
stent or near its edge, doctors call it

7
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:27,423
in-stent restenosis. Tissue can build up
inside the stent.

8
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:30,952
Sometimes the stent itself did not open
fully.

9
00:00:31,463 --> 00:00:34,957
The cause matters because it helps
determine which treatment the team

10
00:00:35,027 --> 00:00:35,828
chooses.

11
00:00:36,269 --> 00:00:40,983
An angiogram uses contrast and X-rays to
show the narrowed channel.

12
00:00:41,424 --> 00:00:46,485
The team may also use imaging from inside
the artery to see how the stent opened and

13
00:00:46,555 --> 00:00:51,791
what’s inside it. When treatment goes
ahead, a thin coronary guidewire

14
00:00:51,861 --> 00:00:56,354
crosses the narrowed segment and provides
a track for the balloon catheters.

15
00:00:57,051 --> 00:00:59,825
First, the team prepares the narrowed
segment.

16
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:05,085
In this example, a separate preparation
balloon goes over the wire and expands

17
00:01:05,154 --> 00:01:06,559
inside the old stent.

18
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,157
The team deflates and removes that
balloon, then checks the opening and blood

19
00:01:11,203 --> 00:01:16,358
flow. The guidewire stays in place while
the team decides whether to proceed with

20
00:01:16,381 --> 00:01:17,972
the drug-coated balloon.

21
00:01:19,272 --> 00:01:22,825
The drug-coated balloon travels over the
same wire.

22
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:26,087
The medicine is on the outside of the
balloon.

23
00:01:26,691 --> 00:01:31,347
At the treatment site, the team inflates
it so the coating contacts the inner

24
00:01:31,428 --> 00:01:33,344
surface of the treated segment.

25
00:01:33,948 --> 00:01:36,769
Some of the medicine transfers into the
tissue.

26
00:01:37,152 --> 00:01:41,018
Its purpose is to reduce the chance of the
artery narrowing again.

27
00:01:41,529 --> 00:01:44,606
The team deflates and removes the coated
balloon.

28
00:01:44,849 --> 00:01:47,194
The original stent stays in place.

29
00:01:47,798 --> 00:01:53,127
The team takes more contrast X-rays to see
how open the treated area is and how

30
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:54,752
blood flows beyond it.

31
00:01:55,356 --> 00:01:59,547
If the result is inadequate, the team may
need to use a different treatment.

32
00:02:00,244 --> 00:02:05,271
A drug-coated balloon is one option for
selected cases of in-stent restenosis.

33
00:02:05,782 --> 00:02:10,936
In twenty twenty-four, the United States
Food and Drug Administration approved one

34
00:02:11,006 --> 00:02:13,015
coronary device for that use.

35
00:02:13,827 --> 00:02:18,448
Researchers have also studied these
balloons in some small coronary arteries

36
00:02:18,599 --> 00:02:20,340
that had never been stented.

37
00:02:20,944 --> 00:02:24,055
Approved uses vary by country and device.

38
00:02:24,497 --> 00:02:28,827
After the catheters are removed, the care
team controls bleeding at the wrist or

39
00:02:28,897 --> 00:02:31,230
groin and monitors recovery.

40
00:02:31,741 --> 00:02:36,199
Follow your own discharge instructions,
including the plan for antiplatelet

41
00:02:36,257 --> 00:02:40,611
medicines. Check with your cardiology team
before changing them.

42
00:02:41,052 --> 00:02:45,034
Get emergency help for severe or
persistent chest pain or bleeding that

43
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:45,928
won’t stop.

44
00:02:46,369 --> 00:02:49,620
The coated balloon delivers medicine and
then comes out.

45
00:02:50,224 --> 00:02:55,146
In the example you’ve seen, the original
stent stays, and the cardiology team uses

46
00:02:55,204 --> 00:02:58,327
the final images to guide what happens
next.
